= Privacy Policy =
**Last updated:** 18 September 2026
**Effective from:** 18 September 2026
**Version:** 1.1

== At a glance ==

BestWorkplace is a public, static documentation site. It has no accounts, forms, payments, advertising, or public visitor statistics.

The site uses a private page counter to understand which documentation pages are used. It stores only an aggregate total for each page, without a visitor identifier. It does not use analytics cookies or create a browser profile.

== 1. Controller and scope ==

**Controller:** Robert Schaub, In Lederäcker 11, 8305 Dietlikon, Switzerland.

Privacy requests can be sent in writing to this address. This notice covers the BestWorkplace website, its public GitHub repository, the private page counter, and direct project correspondence. External websites have their own privacy notices.

== 2. What happens when you use the site ==

* **Website delivery:** GitHub Pages receives the IP address and ordinary request information needed to deliver and secure the site.
* **Fonts, diagrams, and remote media:** Google Fonts, cdnjs/Cloudflare, and a linked media host receive ordinary request information when their content is loaded.
* **Private page counter:** The internal page reference, prefixed with the BestWorkplace site ID ##BW##, is sent to a Cloudflare Worker. Cloudflare receives ordinary network information, including the IP address, but the Worker writes only the aggregate page total to Workers KV. It does not store the IP address, a cookie, or another visitor identifier. Only the operator can view the totals through the authenticated Cloudflare account. There is no public statistics endpoint or visible counter. The viewer removes the retired ##fh_vid## value if an earlier version left it in the browser.
* **GitHub and correspondence:** Public contributions retain the GitHub identity and contribution history. If you contact the operator, the message and contact details are used to answer and handle the request.

These data are used only to deliver and secure the site, maintain and improve the documentation, count aggregate page use, and respond to requests. They are not sold or used for advertising or individual profiling.

== 3. Providers and processing abroad ==

GitHub, Google, and Cloudflare may process request information outside Switzerland, including in the United States. They determine some website-delivery and service-log processing under their own terms. Cloudflare processes the page reference and aggregate totals for the operator under its customer data-processing terms. Where the operator is responsible for an international transfer, the applicable recognised safeguard is used, such as a relevant Data Privacy Framework certification or recognised standard contractual clauses.

Provider information:

* [[GitHub Privacy Statement>>https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement]]
* [[Google Privacy Policy>>https://policies.google.com/privacy]]
* [[Cloudflare Privacy Policy>>https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/]]

== 4. Retention ==

* Aggregate page totals are kept while useful for maintaining the documentation and reviewed at least annually. They contain no visitor identifier.
* Direct correspondence is normally kept for up to two years after the matter is closed, unless law, a dispute, or a documented security need requires longer.
* Public GitHub history may remain in the repository, forks, clones, releases, or archives.
* GitHub, Google, Cloudflare, and remote media hosts set the retention periods for their own service logs.

== 5. Your rights and changes ==

Depending on the applicable law and circumstances, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, or objection by writing to the controller. Identity or authority may be verified before data are disclosed or changed. The operator aims to provide an initial response within 30 days.

Public Git history cannot always be removed from distributed copies, but reasonable correction, redaction, deletion, or platform measures will be assessed. You may also contact the [[Swiss Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC)>>https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/en]].

The site uses HTTPS, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security. Do not place secrets or unnecessary personal data in public GitHub contributions.

Material changes to this notice will be versioned and dated. The notice will be reviewed before forms, visitor identifiers, public statistics, or materially different analytics are introduced.
